From: zenlte local fix (v3)
Subject: [PATCH] f2fs-tools: never stamp feature bits the 3.10 kernel cannot parse

Apply in: src/external/f2fs-tools

ROOT CAUSE OF THE v1/v2 f2fs PANIC.

f2fs-tools here is 1.16.0.  Its CONF_ANDROID default set ("make_f2fs -g android",
which is exactly how fs_mgr and recovery invoke it) enabled:

    ENCRYPT (0x0001)  - kernel knows this
    QUOTA_INO (0x0080), PRJQUOTA (0x0010), EXTRA_ATTR (0x0008), VERITY (0x0400)
                      - all UNKNOWN to this device's kernel

The zenlte kernel is 3.10 and knows exactly two feature bits
(kernel/samsung/universal7420/include/linux/f2fs_fs.h:112-113):
    F2FS_FEATURE_ENCRYPT   0x0001
    F2FS_FEATURE_BLKZONED  0x0002
and its struct f2fs_inode is the pre-4.14 fixed layout with NO i_extra_isize.

f2fs has no incompatible-feature gate, so the old kernel mounts the filesystem
anyway.  With EXTRA_ATTR set, mkfs writes block pointers at
i_addr[get_extra_isize()] while the kernel reads i_addr[0] -- so the kernel
consumes inode metadata as block addresses.  Those garbage addresses reach
update_sit_entry(), which indexes sit_i->sentries[segno] with no bounds check,
~700x out of bounds -> kernel panic on the first fdatasync().

Corroboration: the TWRP tree ships f2fs-tools 1.14.0, whose CONF_ANDROID does
NOT set EXTRA_ATTR -- which is why TWRP-formatted f2fs worked and
ROM-formatted f2fs did not.

TWO changes here, and BOTH are required:

  1. The CONF_ANDROID default set keeps only ENCRYPT.
  2. An authoritative mask applied AFTER getopt and AFTER the defaults.
     This second part is essential and is NOT optional: fs_mgr and recovery
     both pass an explicit "-O project_quota,extra_attr" on the command line
     (fs_mgr's needs_projid is a hardcoded `true`), so fixing the defaults
     alone would have left the bug fully intact.

DEVICE SPECIFIC: correct because this tree only ever builds zenlte.  On a
multi-device tree this must be gated on the target kernel version.

diff --git a/mkfs/f2fs_format_main.c b/mkfs/f2fs_format_main.c
index f3316f7..42d7162 100644
--- a/mkfs/f2fs_format_main.c
+++ b/mkfs/f2fs_format_main.c
@@ -111,7 +111,9 @@ static void f2fs_show_info()
 }
 
 #if defined(ANDROID_TARGET) && defined(HAVE_SYS_UTSNAME_H)
-static bool kernel_version_over(unsigned int min_major, unsigned int min_minor)
+/* zenlte: retained for reference, but unused -- see add_default_options() */
+static bool __attribute__((unused))
+kernel_version_over(unsigned int min_major, unsigned int min_minor)
 {
 	unsigned int major, minor;
 	struct utsname uts;
@@ -126,7 +128,8 @@ static bool kernel_version_over(unsigned int min_major, unsigned int min_minor)
 	return false;
 }
 #else
-static bool kernel_version_over(unsigned int UNUSED(min_major),
+static bool __attribute__((unused))
+kernel_version_over(unsigned int UNUSED(min_major),
 				unsigned int UNUSED(min_minor))
 {
 	return false;
@@ -147,13 +150,32 @@ static void add_default_options(void)
 		if (c.feature & F2FS_FEATURE_RO)
 			return;
 
-		/* -O encrypt -O project_quota,extra_attr,{quota} -O verity */
+		/*
+		 * zenlte (Exynos7420) local change -- DEVICE SPECIFIC.
+		 *
+		 * This tree only ever builds zenlte (SM-G928F), whose kernel
+		 * is 3.10 and whose f2fs understands exactly two feature
+		 * bits: ENCRYPT (0x1) and BLKZONED (0x2).  Its
+		 * struct f2fs_inode is the pre-4.14 fixed layout with no
+		 * i_extra_isize member.
+		 *
+		 * Stamping EXTRA_ATTR makes mkfs write block pointers at
+		 * i_addr[get_extra_isize()] while that kernel reads
+		 * i_addr[0], so the kernel interprets inode metadata as
+		 * block addresses.  Those garbage addresses reach
+		 * update_sit_entry(), which indexes sit_i->sentries[segno]
+		 * unchecked -> out-of-bounds access -> kernel panic.
+		 * f2fs has no incompatible-feature gate, so the old kernel
+		 * mounts the filesystem instead of refusing it.
+		 *
+		 * Only ENCRYPT is kept.  PRJQUOTA / QUOTA_INO / VERITY are
+		 * dropped as well: all are unknown to this kernel, and
+		 * PRJQUOTA implies EXTRA_ATTR.
+		 *
+		 * On a multi-device tree this MUST be gated on the target
+		 * kernel version rather than applied unconditionally.
+		 */
 		c.feature |= F2FS_FEATURE_ENCRYPT;
-		if (!kernel_version_over(4, 14))
-			c.feature |= F2FS_FEATURE_QUOTA_INO;
-		c.feature |= F2FS_FEATURE_PRJQUOTA;
-		c.feature |= F2FS_FEATURE_EXTRA_ATTR;
-		c.feature |= F2FS_FEATURE_VERITY;
 		break;
 	}
 #ifdef CONF_CASEFOLD
@@ -316,6 +338,50 @@ static void f2fs_parse_options(int argc, char *argv[])
 
 	add_default_options();
 
+	/*
+	 * zenlte (Exynos7420) local change -- DEVICE SPECIFIC.
+	 *
+	 * Clearing the defaults in add_default_options() is NOT sufficient on
+	 * its own: both callers on this device ask for the killer feature
+	 * explicitly on the command line.
+	 *
+	 *   system/core/fs_mgr/fs_mgr_format.cpp   format_f2fs()
+	 *   bootable/recovery/recovery_utils/roots.cpp  format_volume()
+	 *
+	 * both hardcode "-O project_quota,extra_attr" (fs_mgr's needs_projid
+	 * is a hardcoded `true`), and getopt has already applied those bits
+	 * by the time we get here.
+	 *
+	 * This is therefore the single authoritative choke point -- it runs
+	 * after option parsing AND after the defaults, so it catches every
+	 * caller regardless of what they asked for.  Anything this device's
+	 * 3.10 kernel cannot parse gets masked off, which turns an
+	 * unmountable-but-mounted, panic-on-first-fdatasync filesystem into a
+	 * plain, correct, old-format f2fs.
+	 *
+	 * Kernel side of the contract (the only bits it knows):
+	 *   kernel/samsung/universal7420/include/linux/f2fs_fs.h:112-113
+	 *     F2FS_FEATURE_ENCRYPT   0x0001
+	 *     F2FS_FEATURE_BLKZONED  0x0002
+	 *
+	 * On a multi-device tree this MUST be gated on the target kernel.
+	 */
+	{
+		const uint32_t supported = F2FS_FEATURE_ENCRYPT |
+					   F2FS_FEATURE_BLKZONED;
+		uint32_t dropped = c.feature & ~supported;
+
+		if (dropped) {
+			MSG(0, "Info: zenlte: dropping f2fs feature bits 0x%04x "
+				"unsupported by this device's 3.10 kernel\n",
+				dropped);
+			c.feature &= supported;
+			c.quota_bits = 0;
+			c.s_encoding = 0;
+			c.s_encoding_flags = 0;
+		}
+	}
+
 	if (!(c.feature & F2FS_FEATURE_EXTRA_ATTR)) {
 		if (c.feature & F2FS_FEATURE_PRJQUOTA) {
 			MSG(0, "\tInfo: project quota feature should always be "
